        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "chore(docker): execute Compose and package artifact proofs",
        "body": "Closes #101039\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a problem where the Docker Compose and package-artifact QA scenarios could pass from helper-level assertions without launching the documented Compose services or installing and executing the real package tarball in a target container.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe scenarios now run through the existing Docker scheduler, image catalog, package builder, and shared script-evidence writer. The Compose proof starts the documented Gateway and CLI topology from the package-backed functional image, while the package proof installs the canonical tarball in the scheduler-selected bare image; both record exact package, image, and container identities.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThere is no product runtime change. Release and Docker QA evidence now establishes that the documented Compose topology becomes healthy and that the generated npm package installs and executes in its target container.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox through Crabbox: provider `blacksmith-testbox`, id `tbx_01kww4vxpjqqwhwhtmya593d5r`.\n- Focused validation: targeted oxlint passed; 34 focused Vitest assertions passed; full `tsconfig.projects.json` tsgo build passed.\n- Package proof: `openclaw@2026.6.11`, package sha256 `eb8226bbf2a1f7f80b6ed46fcfffcd4d0240575077c602c8eda0cc7e51bc8179`, bare image `sha256:2b5cee81d762f611961325123ff4b170e2bcfccfdbcd620bd461d0bbae413172`, target container `095f12929afa5c3942b75703b61b3d9778c6b7a24d8c1dd43f91f175622628cb`; installed CLI version and help commands passed.\n- Compose proof after package/image binding fix: package sha256 `5864bf22daa02fe4c2a35119907d4d6a9972f0d4edf0580c15e91f2bd946b1c4`, functional image `sha256:bc8065698f2674f4ad1bfa2de5c2fa076cfbd041ad6c24bdcc524fea310446c1`, Gateway container `ad66568384bb1211400317fbca107a3e18eaf6a502378b115301c44421e3382b`, CLI container `328d2d7485704b84e65d4659fc9bd2ec1828b4dc4317901d72e5c5ee7aafca38`; Gateway health and CLI health commands passed.\n- Fresh branch autoreview against `origin/main`: clean, with no accepted/actionable findings.\n\nAI-assisted change; implementation and evidence were reviewed and validated as described above.\n",
